   "versionNonce": 700952,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Consistency chosen over availability - affordable only because of a protocol from 1982",
   "originalText": "Consistency chosen over availability - affordable only because of a protocol from 1982",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2132,
   "width": 1003,
   "height": 178,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100137,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700959,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "message content              IMMUTABLE once written        content-addressed, so the hash IS the identity: no consistency\n                                                           question can arise, because a hash always maps to the same bytes\nper-recipient metadata row   STRONG within its partition   a message acknowledged with 250 OK must be durably present.\n                                                           Quorum writes.\nis_read / is_starred / labels  EVENTUAL, last-write-wins   two devices setting the same boolean write the same value, so LWW\n                                                           is CORRECT rather than a compromise - no coordination needed\nfolder_id (a move)           EVENTUAL, last-write-wins     two devices moving one message resolve to one winner, pushed to\n                                                           both over WebSocket. A conflict-resolution UI would be worse.\nunread_by_folder             EVENTUAL w.r.t. the main table  denormalized; drifts on partial failure, repaired by recompute\nunread_count                 EVENTUAL, drifts              incrementally maintained, periodically recomputed\nsearch index                 EVENTUAL, seconds behind      async, with a hybrid recent-message scan to cover the gap",
   "originalText": "message content              IMMUTABLE once written        content-addressed, so the hash IS the identity: no consistency\n                                                           question can arise, because a hash always maps to the same bytes\nper-recipient metadata row   STRONG within its partition   a message acknowledged with 250 OK must be durably present.\n                                                           Quorum writes.\nis_read / is_starred / labels  EVENTUAL, last-write-wins   two devices setting the same boolean write the same value, so LWW\n                                                           is CORRECT rather than a compromise - no coordination needed\nfolder_id (a move)           EVENTUAL, last-write-wins     two devices moving one message resolve to one winner, pushed to\n                                                           both over WebSocket. A conflict-resolution UI would be worse.\nunread_by_folder             EVENTUAL w.r.t. the main table  denormalized; drifts on partial failure, repaired by recompute\nunread_count                 EVENTUAL, drifts              incrementally maintained, periodically recomputed\nsearch index                 EVENTUAL, seconds behind      async, with a hybrid recent-message scan to cover the gap",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2372,
   "width": 995,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100138,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700966,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Because 'data loss is unacceptable' outranks availability, a metadata partition that loses quorum STOPS SERVING rather than\naccepting writes it might lose. So during a failover, affected users briefly cannot read or receive mail - and that is the\ncorrect trade, because SMTP senders will retry for days. THE PROTOCOL'S OWN RETRY BEHAVIOUR IS WHAT MAKES CHOOSING\nCONSISTENCY AFFORDABLE, which is a nice example of a constraint from 1982 buying you something.",
   "originalText": "Because 'data loss is unacceptable' outranks availability, a metadata partition that loses quorum STOPS SERVING rather than\naccepting writes it might lose. So during a failover, affected users briefly cannot read or receive mail - and that is the\ncorrect trade, because SMTP senders will retry for days. THE PROTOCOL'S OWN RETRY BEHAVIOUR IS WHAT MAKES CHOOSING\nCONSISTENCY AFFORDABLE, which is a nice example of a constraint from 1982 buying you something.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
